@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+**First read.** The eye lands first on the large serif headline, "Hire a narrowboat for a week on the canal". It then goes to the dark green Search button in the white "Find a boat" card. It reads as a quiet, honest booking page for a small boatyard, with clear type and one clear action. On phone and tablet the card moves under the intro and the routes list moves under the card. The order stays the same and is easy to follow.
+
+**What it's for.** To get a visitor to search for and book a narrowboat week directly with the boatyard.
+
+**Verdict.** This round's fix lines up the routes list on tablet. It added nothing new and broke nothing. The biggest gap is the same as before: the page sells a week on the water but shows no boat and no canal. Only the maker can supply that photo.
+
+**Finding status**
+- no-image-of-boats-or-water: open. There is still no photo of a boat, lock or canal at any viewport. There is still about 190 px of empty space under the content on desktop and about 470 px on widescreen.
+- start-date-no-year: open. The Start date field still shows "Sat 14 June", with no year and no calendar icon, at all four viewports.
+- tablet-routes-list-narrow: closed. On tablet the rules of the routes list now end at x 720. That is the right edge of the form card and the nav (before, they ended at x 688).
+
+**New problems.** None. The desktop and widescreen images are the same as before. The facts file shows no contrast, target-size or line-length violations at any viewport.
+
+**What would move it most**
+1. The page shows no boat or water. This is the whole page; on desktop and widescreen, put the photo in the empty band below the content. The visitor is booking a week on a canal, but sees only text and form fields, so the copy must carry all the feeling of the trip. Add one real photo of this company's boats or of one of the routes, and keep the form where it is. The maker must supply the photo. Taste. Viewports: desktop, phone, tablet, widescreen.
+
+**Smaller things.**
+- The Start date field in the search card says "Sat 14 June", with no year and no sign that it opens a date picker. Show the year, or add a calendar icon. Viewports: desktop, phone, tablet, widescreen.
+
+**What's working.**
+- The routes list gives each route in nights and locks ("7 nights, 38 locks"). This is real, specific data that helps a visitor choose. At every viewport its right edge now lines up with the edges above it.
